  "narrative": {
    "intro": "DDB Chicago obligated $303M in federal contract funding in FY2026 to date across 11 awards, with an average award size of $27.6M. Obligations are down 22.4% year over year. Historical obligations show a peak in FY23 at $596M, then stepped down through FY24 at $399M and FY25 at $391M before the current-year total of $303M. Award activity has been concentrated into a relatively small number of high-value awards: 11 awards produced the current-year total, which drives the $27.6M average award size. The current-year total is a fiscal year to date figure and therefore partial. Readers tracking DDB Chicago should note the year-to-year variability in obligations: FY21 was $348M, FY22 was $363M, FY23 was $596M, FY24 was $399M, FY25 was $391M, and FY26 is $303M so far.",
