        "heading": "What explains the year-over-year change in obligations?",
        "body": "DDB Chicago obligations are down 22.4% year over year. Fiscal-year comparisons show FY23 at $596M as the high point, followed by lower totals in FY24 at $399M, FY25 at $391M, and FY26 at $303M to date. The decline reflects smaller total obligations rather than a change in award count, since the current year includes 11 awards with an average award size of $27.6M."
      },
